# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QLNN_d3d_1 — TGLF settings of the training database (DIII-D,
# production_run_4 / sat3_em_azf-1 corpus, Jul 2026).
#
# The switches in the "database settings" block were forced onto every case
# by the database generator on top of the ig2it-generated
# input.tglf: SAT_RULE=3 in CGYRO units, electromagnetic (USE_BPER/USE_BPAR),
# ALPHA_ZF=-1, NBASIS_MAX=6, KYGRID_MODEL=4 / NKY=12, NMODES=2,
# USE_MHD_RULE=false, USE_AVE_ION_GRID=false. A QLNN prediction is only
# meaningful with these settings: the QL weights were computed with them, and
# run_qlnn feeds them through TJLF's saturation rule with the SAT_RULE /
# ALPHA_ZF / UNITS of the input it is given, so pass them as here.
#
# Species layout: NS=3 (1 = e, 2 = D, 3 = carbon with MASS_3 forced to 6.0),
# i.e. the standard DIII-D (e, D, C) truncation. The nets read 32 inputs
# (no USE_AVE_ION_GRID feature, no ky-grid canonicalisation); an NS=3 input
# is used as is. NS > 3 inputs are NOT lumped for this bundle.
#
# VEXB_SHEAR: the ig2it inputs of this corpus were generated before the
# mid-2026 sign fix (vexb_convention = legacy), so VEXB_SHEAR here is
# opposite in sign to VPAR_SHEAR_1 (TGYRO convention would be same-sign).
# TurbulentTransport applies the SIGN_BT flip for legacy bundles itself.
#
# Physics values below are a real DIII-D case from the database (ModeID
# summary row 33018, case id 14211620000.5 = DIII-D shot 142116; r/R = 0.208,
# nominal operating point). VPAR/VPAR_SHEAR of species 2-3 are set equal to
# species 1 as ig2it does. Replace them with your own; keep the switches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

